== (4) density covered by the three integer-cycle rules at precision K ==
 K = 12 bits: three integer rules cover density 3 * 2^-12 = 7.32e-04 of all integers; the no-descent residual at ~K/1.58 Syracuse steps is of order 10^-2..10^-3 (D(k) table): aperiodic words dominate
 K = 24 bits: three integer rules cover density 3 * 2^-24 = 1.79e-07 of all integers; the no-descent residual at ~K/1.58 Syracuse steps is of order 10^-2..10^-3 (D(k) table): aperiodic words dominate
 K = 40 bits: three integer rules cover density 3 * 2^-40 = 2.73e-12 of all integers; the no-descent residual at ~K/1.58 Syracuse steps is of order 10^-2..10^-3 (D(k) table): aperiodic words dominate
 K = 64 bits: three integer rules cover density 3 * 2^-64 = 1.63e-19 of all integers; the no-descent residual at ~K/1.58 Syracuse steps is of order 10^-2..10^-3 (D(k) table): aperiodic words dominate
